 R←Test_003(debugFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;ns;qdmx
⍝ Exercise the optional left argument of `Notify`: with `noTrap` being 1 the error is not
⍝ trapped but passed on, which is what makes the function debuggable.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 ns←⎕NS''                                       ⍝ No `TatinVars` in here
 {}ns.⎕FX ##.WindowsToast.⎕NR'Notify'

 :Trap 6
     {}1 ns.Notify'YesOrNo' 'Test_003: nobody should ever see this'
     →T.GoToTidyUp 1                            ⍝ The error must have reached us
 :Else
     qdmx←⎕DMX
     →T.GoToTidyUp 6≠qdmx.EN
 :EndTrap
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠ns.⎕NC'∆NotifyError'           ⍝ Nothing was trapped, so nothing was recorded

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
⍝Done
